<p>My name is Emeric Braud, and I am a software developer.</p>

<p>Here I write about the programming lessons learned from building <a href="https://github.com/EmericBraud/alcyon">Alcyon</a>, a chess engine in C++23: multithreaded alpha-beta search, NNUE evaluation, bitboards, and the measurement work that tells whether an optimization really is one.</p>

<p>The engine's source code is open: <a href="https://github.com/EmericBraud/alcyon">github.com/EmericBraud/alcyon</a>.</p>
